{
 "_comment": "tiny-chat size arm, seed 2 at 150m_L8 (experiments/tiny_chat_2026-10/PREREGISTRATION.md amendment 6): the CUDA gate on this machine's GPU, the gate (design final, the floor pilot's PASS, experiments/tiny_chat_2026-10/size/stage0/cuda_gate_150m_L8.json passed, experiments/tiny_chat_2026-10/size/plain_bitid.json ok, the pretraining lr equal to experiments/tiny_chat_2026-10/stage0/lr_choice_150m.json's; here 0.0005), the 35% data job, 10000 steps x 16384 tokens at batch 16 x accum 2, rungs at [500, 1000, 2500, 5000] in the light slot (cache capped at 2048 MB), and the post job (SFT at the same micro-batching, panels, Carry-5 with ember generation, base-model Carry-5), which brings home its per-item records, replies and SFT model. One GPU job at a time. Estimated 10.4 L4 VM-hours. The pick runs at home once all three seeds are home: python tools/colab_chat/tiny_chat_run.py pick --out ART/e1_150m/pick_e1_150m_L8 --run ART/e1_150m_r1/post_e1_150m_L8_r1 --run ART/e1_150m_r2/post_e1_150m_L8_r2 --run ART/e1_150m_r3/post_e1_150m_L8_r3. Upload vocab_llama3_bpe.gguf with the runner's --upload. Carry-5 generation (24 Oct 2026, PREREGISTRATION.md implementation note): ember.cpp's CUDA server at aa50a6112dfd (cloned and built once per VM by the first post job, under a lock), on the SFT model's F32 GGUF; every post job first generates 40 fixed items with ember and with mtstudio chat and lets ember generate only on 40/40 identical replies, else mtstudio for the whole run (gen_flag in its summary.json). Forced-choice scoring stays with mtstudio score. Dialogue levels [0, 17, 35, 70]% (copies), E1 at 35% (design.json final).",
 "max_parallel": 1,
 "max_parallel_light": 1,
